hey guys Pete here this will be my mr.  robot season 4 episode to recap and  review we got some answers that ask some  questions then a slow simmering kind of  character based episode and then a last  minute reveal that has major  implications for the rest of the story  if you haven't watched episode 2 of mr.  robots fourth season which is titled 402  payment required then this video will be  filled with spoilers and it's not for  you hit the subscribe button go watch  the episode and then come back for this  because we're gonna talk about  everything that happened for everyone  else let's get into it four words in a  room we've seen before no the other one  imaginary magda Alderson an imaginary  younger Elliot knows something that we  don't based on the end of episode 2 it's  something that mr. robot and Elliot  don't know either there's another  personality lurking inside Elliot and  that is the bomb that this episode  dropped and Wow that's a lot to think  about this isn't an idea that hasn't  come up over and over in series Sam s  Mel told The Hollywood Reporter in an  interview that he scans the forums and  he hasn't seen this particular twist  guessed correctly yet since this is the  thing that's on everybody's minds I  promise that we'll come back to it at  the end of the video and we'll talk a  lot more about it and more about what  Sam said in that interview but a lot of  other things did happen in this episode  and we can't just overlook them so first  and foremost we get an education on the  dais group from Phillip price the  sequence of events picks up right after  he revives Elliot the sequence really  brought home to me how well this show is  put together because let's face it this  could have easily come off as lame or  cheesy if they didn't get it absolutely  right  I think they pulled it off and in the  process of that we learned that in 1989  after the fall of the Berlin Wall a  young imaginative Minister Jiang aka  White Rose saw a possibility for a new  world order  Jane created an investment group with a  goal of bringing together the world's  wealthiest and most powerful men to  consolidate control and manipulate  events for profit turns out that a  younger White Rose  very good at recruiting and the  potential profits were such that they  trumped anybody's moral reservations  about being involved in these kinds of  activities what the group members  including price failed to recognize  though was that white rose had a bigger  plan in mind  a secret billion dollar project which we  know is under the Washington Township  plant where Elliott's father worked that  project which we can't say for sure what  it is is currently being shipped off to  the Congo and when that happens price  and Elliott will no longer be abuse for  white rose in his story about the dais  group and how they came together there's  a truckload of exposition for us as  viewers and Elliott who is essentially a  dead man walking  Ecore panned the dark army were on the  radar but this is the first introduction  of dais  fortunately for Elliott all roads lead  back to White Rose which is where all  his energy has been focused anyway but  the group makes her seem even more  powerful if that's possible as we watch  the clips with her shaking hands with  world leaders Elliott and contrast is  sitting in his old office at allsafe  which is kind of boarded up and  abandoned he's essentially talking to  himself as he talks to mr. robot so even  though price decides to help him the  odds are completely stacked against  these two elsewhere we do see that Dom  has followed Janice's directions and  made it to her meeting about the  Santiago case the way this scene played  out really worked for me as I bought her  performance and thought she was actually  turning on the dark army as that was  playing out this doesn't turn out to be  the case though rather she's just  feeding the investigating agent a dark  army approved cover story about Santiago  working with a drug cartel  Janice is awesome again she continues to  carve out a space in the story at the  late stage that she's entered it when  Dom says she can only be 99% certain  that they bought her story the agent  dies it's made to look like a suicide  but it's clear that the dark army made  this happen he's thrown from his balcony  at his apartment or hotel or whatever it  was and I just have to point it out once  again DOM does a fantastic job here and  her situation is really emphasized here  it kind of gets put in the background of  the big story that's going on but the  dark army is really putting the squeeze  on her Elliott is also up against the  clock here we know there's 8 days until  the project ships he needs White Rose to  bring the Deus group together price  helps out with this he goes and meets  with White Rose tells them he's going to  resign and that they have to replace him  we learned that they have to get the  whole group together in order to do that  before he goes and does that we learned  that Susan Jacobs who Darlene killed  obviously in season 2 was his connection  with the banking so while price goes off  to meet with White Rose Elliott tries to  figure out how to get a hold of Susan  Jacobs in episode 1 Elliott and Darlene  were at odds with each other  she was self-medicating and accusing him  of shutting down in response to Angela's  death we find out in this episode that  their mother has died which ultimately  brings them back together  it's a strange term but I think it's an  interesting one because Elliott is  laser-focused here the stakes are life  and death for him and his sister she  doesn't know that yet but he has to take  time out they both do to deal with this  real family situation and of course they  don't like their mother their mother was  not a good parent but we get some good  character moments with them here  especially when they listen to the tape  and what this whole sequence this whole  situation of dealing with her in the  funeral home it really built anxiety  like as a viewer for me I was anxious  that like the episode was gonna come to  an end and I knew something was gonna  have to happen so I think it ultimately  worked for me but it felt strange when I  was watching it the first time it does  serve the purpose of getting Darlene and  Elliott together I think that's a good  thing  I think Darlene brings some humanity  into the situation where Elliott's just  only focused on what he's thinking and  what he's trying to do I think what she  says is important as well he does need  her in order to do this like I mentioned  a few minutes ago the odds are  completely stacked against these guys so  they're able to take care of the  situation with their mother they're able  to talk about Angela and get that out in  the open  now they're both working together which  is a good thing  Elliot learns that she killed Susan  Jacobs and he's upset at first but he  forgives her for doing what she did  because of the things that Susan Jacobs  did in relation to the Washington  Township case as they're talking she  mentions that Veera is back which we saw  in the post credit scene of season  three's finale she also mentions when  she brought up Vera's return to Eliot he  brushed it all this leads to Eliot and  mr. robot having a confrontation where  they both say that they don't remember  the conversation and it opens the door  to there being another personality with  whom Angela had told this information to  then we cut back to the boardroom where  Eliot first had his meeting with Tyrell  there we find his mother and a younger  version of himself there's a table that  has four chairs there we find out that  they're waiting for someone they're not  waiting for Elliot they're not waiting  for mr. robot they're waiting for the  other one and that brings us to the end  of the episode and to the big question  of who is the other personality I think  it's interesting here how they  introduced that like we had a Corp and  the dark army and now we learned that  there is a Deus group that's behind them  in the same way we had Elliot and mr.  robot they were at odds with each other  but then we also learned that there's  another personality that's another layer  beyond them so there's a pretty nice  parallel between those two situations  there in the beginning of the series  Elliot told us there was a powerful  group of people running the world now at  the beginning of season four we find out  about this Deus group who fit this  opening description from the pilot to a  tee there's a powerful group of people  out there that are secretly running the  world  I'm talking about the guys no one knows  about the guys that are invisible the  top 1% of the top 1% the guys that play  God without permission it's nice to go  back to the beginning and to get this  reveal to speculate about but if I'm  being honest I don't have a good guess  at what is happening my first thought  was that we are the other personality  Eliot talks to us as his imaginary  friend  are plenty of reasons why that wouldn't  exactly make sense in the hollywood  reporter interview s mail says that this  idea was baked in since the beginning of  the story he says when it's revealed  that we will absolutely be able to go  back through the series and see it he  says and I'm quoting here I think it's  one of those things where if we did our  job right it's a balance of it feeling  inevitable but also unexpected and  surprising that's what we're going for  we don't want to be too much of a shock  where it's just a gotcha and a gimmick  type of twist moment we wanted to feel  earned because the answer should make  sense  you guys could technically figure it out  because it's been in the show the whole  time we're excited to see it play out so  now the table is officially set and it  looks like Sam in the writers room have  strived to keep it a hundred percent  this episode had a little bit of  everything there were some funny parts  slipped in there with Darlene and Eliot  cremation cardboard coffin your cheapest  urn the guy in the snowman costume  offering condolences Dom situation on  the other hand is not funny  it's the pressure cooker where her  family will pay if she doesn't perform  for the dark army and Janice really adds  some color they're learning about Deus  is satisfying and it makes you wonder  how things will shake out for price it's  unlikely that this new Alliance is going  to end well for both price and Elliot  and as viewers do we actually want to  see the guy who was the face of evil  Corp get a happy ending  birra has yet to make an appearance but  we at least have some context around the  end credits scene now he's been in both  the trailers so I'm sure it's just a  matter of time until we see the brave  traveler inject himself into the current  events we also didn't get any Tyrell but  he should also make a return rather soon  episode 2 was another great looking  episode there were good character  moments with Elliot and Darlene enough  mystery to go around wTF is going on in  that boardroom and where exactly is that  going down I mean it's in Elliott's head  but where does the body if you get where  I'm coming from there's so much to think  about so much to discuss let me know in  the comments what you think's going on  and where things are headed there are  plenty of details for us to discuss and  I'll be interested to see what you guys  are thinking please like the video if  you enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel  if you haven't already thanks for  watching we'll talk to you soon
 

